  "change_claim": {
    "affected_components": [],
    "architecture_delta": "A new xtask module (corpus) holding the manifest types and their validation. No runner, no new dependency: the manifest is TOML, read by the toml crate xtask already uses.",
    "contract_changes": "none: no product component exists",
    "intent": "Commit xtask/tests/corpus/manifest.toml with every case of plan §6 — id, level, seeded description, rule, §4.1 cell, expected outcome — and the directory skeleton, before any checker code exists. The manifest is declarative enough that CHG-004 generates each crate-level fixture workspace from it rather than from committed copies (Kennedy, 2026-09-19).",
    "non_goals": [
      "Checker code: `cargo xtask architecture` stays the stub it is until CHG-003",
      "The generator itself, `cargo xtask corpus run`, and the fixture workspaces: CHG-004 at crate level, CHG-007 at module level",
      "Module-level fixtures. The module cases are pre-registered here and built in CHG-007",
      "Editing rha-crates.toml, the root workspace, or any protected surface other than adding the manifest to [surface] protected",
      "Kennedy's held-out cases, which live outside this repository and which the Executor must not read or write (§9.14)"
    ],
    "performance_impact": "none claimed",
    "source": {
      "path": ".rha/tasks/CHG-002-corpus-pre-registration.toml",
      "sha256": "328fac8fca461ad9fe75503147c03f6fee818d6f46e885b4c54869147d394f95"
    },
    "task": "CHG-002",
    "unresolved": [
      "L0.architecture is still not_run and is required and non-waivable (DP-0.5), so this change cannot be Eligible either (CHG-001 acceptance, carried_forward 1).",
      "DP-1.1: Kennedy reviews the manifest and authors two or three held-out crate-level cases outside this repository. The held-out cases are the only part of H4 the Executor does not write, and they are what make the acceptance more than self-assessment."
    ]
  },
